        "color": "amber",
        "collapsed": false,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 150,
        "body": "**Molar Mass** reads a formula (H₂O is about 18 g/mol), and the **Moles ↔ Mass** equation turns 36 g of water into moles. **pH** is −log₁₀ of the hydrogen-ion concentration: 0.001 mol/L gives pH 3. **Dilution** and **half-life** below; the **Element** card looks up iron.",
